===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*steygʰ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|steire}}, {{m|enm|staire}}, {{m|enm|stayre}}, {{m|enm|stayer}}, {{m|enm|steir}}, {{m|enm|steyre}}, {{m|enm|steyer}}, from {{inh|en|ang|stǣġer|t=stair, staircase}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*staigriz|t=stairs, scaffolding}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*steygʰ-|t=to walk, proceed, march, climb}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|steiger||a stair, step, wharf, pier, scaffolding}}, {{cog|gml|steiger}}, {{m|gml|steir||scaffolding}}, {{cog|nds-de|Steiger||a scaffold; trestle}}. Related to {{cog|ang|āstǣġan||to ascend, go up, embark}}, {{cog|ang|stīġan||to go, move, reach; ascend, mount, go up, spring up, rise; scale}}, {{cog|de|Stiege||a flight of stairs}}. More at {{m|en|sty}}.

